# gnome-keyring — the system's Secret Service (org.freedesktop.secrets), i.e. the
# API every libsecret client stores logins through: Claude Code, VS Code,
# Electron/Chromium apps, and proton-vpn-gtk-app itself.
#
# It was ALREADY on the ISO, but only as a transitive dependency
# (proton-vpn-gtk-app -> python-proton-keyring-linux -> gnome-keyring). Listing it
# explicitly means dropping or re-working Proton VPN can never silently take the
# whole system's keyring with it.
#
# Arch's stock /etc/pam.d/sddm and sddm-autologin already carry
# `-auth/-session optional pam_gnome_keyring.so auto_start`, so the keyring is
# unlocked with the login password with no PAM patching from us. /etc/pam.d/passwd
# (shipped in airootfs) adds the matching password-change hook.
#
# NOTE: kwallet ALSO provides org.freedesktop.secrets — see the apiEnabled=false
# note in maze-plasma-config's /etc/skel/.config/kwalletrc for why exactly one of
# the two is allowed to own the name.
gnome-keyring
filelight
partitionmanager
kdeconnect
